Today is Saturday.
It is now eleven o'clock in the morning.
Asha and I meet at a cafe.
We sit and drink coffee.
My calendar is perfectly organized now.
All my tasks happen exactly on time.
Asha asks, "Maya, what do you do every day?"
I say, "I go to the office from Monday to Friday."
"On Tuesday and Thursday I always go to the gym."
Asha asks, "Where do you go on the weekend?"
I say, "I sometimes go to the park."
"Sometimes I ride my bicycle."
"What do you do on the weekend?"
Asha says, "I always rest on the weekend."
"I do not go anywhere."
We laugh.
Today at half past two I have my haircut.
I happily chat with Asha.
